{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages","id":1066206,"title":"How paranoid are your mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T03:05:24-07:00","id":1066206,"title":"How paranoid are your mages?","content":"I am curious about the breadth of experience across the forum on this issue. For some their seems to often be an unspoken assumption that Mages refuse to leave their homes without casting a bevy of protective or divination spells first in the safety of their magically fortified nuclear bunker sanctums. On the one hand I can totally understand this view. Mages are relatively fragile compared to vampires or werewolves and are incredibly aware of how terrifyingly dangerous the world they live in is. If you had all this magic at your disposal, why wouldn't you take steps to protect yourself?<br /> <br /> On the other hand, mages are real people, not automatons, they get lazy, make mistakes or just want to get on with their lives, mages live in a dangerous world but I feel that for most weeks or months may pass for most between dangerous incidents. I don't see many of them checking their cars for bombs every morning before they start the engine or setting up home in an extra-dimensional space rather than renting an apartment. (Very difficult to get good broadband without Forces magic I assume) <br /> <br /> I am in the process of brainstorming ideas for a mage setting, so wanted to gauge how other folks have drawn the line between safety and practicality. What kind of steps do your PCs and NPCs take on a daily basis, on the 6 days out of 7 when they don't know of anyone specifically gunning for them. Do they divine the future and refuse to go to work if anything hazardous is predicted? Do they walk around swathed in layers of potent buffing spells? What about Sanctums and other abodes, do your cabals all live together so they can sleep in a Warded SafeSpace or have their own homes with marginal protection? <br /> <br /> No right or wrong answers, just wanted an insight into how different folk approach this in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T03:40:55-07:00","id":1066221,"title":"","content":"My players are not usually paranoid, but if they know they're going somewhere dangerous, they will load up on the spells. Currently they're pursuing their most hated rival cabal across the universe through a Wending into stranger realms, and they have Shielding spells against insta-kill spells from Life and Death (Unmaking and Making, respectively), a maxed out Wards and Signs, extremely buffed mental and physical stats to increase their defense and initiative to 9+, and the like. They're fighting against Masters and Adepts, and Supernal Dispellation is dangerous. All the protective spells in the world won't do anything when they're all wiped out by a single casting of dispellation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:18:05-07:00","id":1066231,"title":"","content":"For sanity sake, I assume they use up all their spell control slots barring one to maintain magic, plus one or two spells that they relinquish safely or unsafely if they have good way to control it. Spells with duration of less than full day have no drawbacks in releasing then unsafely, too, so if a Mage needs to prepare for something, they will use as many spells as they think it's ok and relinquish unsafely [as long as it's within the same day]. Cabals tend to benefit from group spells, but take note that our game's mage population is smaller than usual so some cabals are single person plus a circle of supporting non mage characters, two mages, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-22-2017, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T04:25:27-07:00","id":1066234,"title":"","content":"Hugely varies, depending on how much enemies the mages made, and what kind of enemies they made. Powerful mages tend to be more paranoid, since their enemies are accordingly more powerful and resourceful, and they've lived just long enough to experience firsthand that the Fallen World has a myriad ways to screw someone's day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:09:18-07:00","id":1066241,"title":"","content":"In my World of Darkness, Pentacle as community is under attack from all sides, all the time. Because of that, mages are naturally cautious. Use of defensive spells is normal. Every mage tries to make his sanctum secure by it being secret, or well-fortified, or both. Teachers try to induce useful habits into their pupils, like divining a close future every morning, or checking on new sympathetic connections daily. Mage communities are built on trust and co-dependency: people will check out on you from time to time, and purely social visits on neutral ground seen as a good practice. Some mages naturally see all this as a nuisance; natural selection usually take care of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:24:35-07:00","id":1066246,"title":"","content":"I admit, I've tended to largely ignore the issue. Getting your Acanthus to spam divination spells is pretty normal, but that's more about it being useful, rather than as threat detection. Mostly, there's just not been much reason to be paranoid in my settings.<br /> <br /> Now contra to that, the players are always very paranoid. Maybe that's the reason; if your players are expecting to be suddenly attacked, it's more interesting to have them repeatedly overreact to non-threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T05:36:27-07:00","id":1066252,"title":"","content":"Depends on game, on character, on much.<br /> Right now I'm in a game with two mages, a beast and an uratha.<br /> It's in an old city, well inhabited by a dozen or so mages (most of them are academics) and all sorts of creatures. Relationships with them are mostly smooth.<br /> The two mages are a public attorney and a cop, paranoia comes naturally.<br /> <br /> And then of course one of the npc mages gets murdered under circumstances no one managed to appraise for weeks right in the middle of our involvement with human traffickers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:24:02-07:00","id":1066272,"title":"","content":"As an Acanthus, I don't think I'm paranoid. I'm a little removed from society, thanks to my filiation to the Mysterium. But I plan acordingly.<br /> If I'm going to venture on a ruin with some cabalmates, we usually use some spells to protect us against ghosts, spirits and stuff like that.<br /> Or if something look particulary dangerous, I use Divination to get some clues. But having somewhat low Gnosis(2) I usually don't walk around overloaded with protection spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:48:25-07:00","id":1066278,"title":"","content":"I tend to feel that Mages are generally quite discreet. They don't walk around covered in protective spells usually, though in uncertain times they may have protections that are specific to a known public issue, and some may do so more often than others. <br /> <br /> But all that said, they do avoid just swanning around in plain sight. Mages prefer for their movements and location to be kept on the down low typically; telling others where a cabal-mate is, that's a bit of a faux pas even if they are an ally. Remember, protective magic can be noticed, and it's often better just not to be spotted at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:20:15-07:00","id":1066293,"title":"","content":"I liked the comparison that I read in the other thread about Mages basically behaving as if they were members of the Mafia or what not.<br /> <br /> They understand that their lives as danger, know that there's some possibility of danger, but it doesn't stop them from living their lives and they can even sometimes get caught off-guard.<br /> <br /> I.e., &quot;basically like normal people, but with a certain amount of heightened awareness.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T07:25:39-07:00","id":1066294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066246#post1066246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I've tended to largely ignore the issue. Getting your Acanthus to spam divination spells is pretty normal, but that's more about it being useful, rather than as threat detection. Mostly, there's just not been much reason to be paranoid in my settings.<br /> <br /> Now contra to that, the players are always very paranoid. Maybe that's the reason; if your players are expecting to be suddenly attacked, it's more interesting to have them repeatedly overreact to non-threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>This describes most of my mage experience too.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I don't want them filling up their spell slots all the time with defense buffs (beyond the expected: one of Mage Armor or stuff like Incognito Presence or Machine Invisibility) because it gets in the way of doing cool shit.<br /> <br /> I <i>want</i> the Obrimos to Imbue shit whenever they feel like it, I <i>want</i> the Mastigos to fuck around with Goetia and day-long portals. I <i>want</i> the Thyrsus to have Fetishes and whatnot.<br /> <br /> As a result, PCs in my games are unusually active compared to &quot;the average NPC Mage&quot; (of course main antagonists are <i>not</i> &quot;the average NPC Mage&quot;.) and the world they play in exists in a sort of equilibrium which they proceed to explore and disturb.<br /> <br /> Yet they still think I'm going to kill their characters at a moment's notice.<br /> <br /> (Okay maybe that one time I made a player's own Tulpa Squad try to kill him because of Havoc had something to to with that, but that's what happens when you let Paradox change your Spell Factors)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:12:43-07:00","id":1066314,"title":"","content":"I embrace ability of Mages to sustain multiple spells. One of reasons for that is the fact that a lot of magic that you can cast from the get go is able of redefining your daily routine and every day life experience, making interesting and big changes to your lifestyle. This means they can be used to emphasize a certain point about NPCs, bring something about them to life in a colorful, visible and touchable fashion, helping define these people sharply and cost efficiently. Tell me what spells do you sustain, and Ill tell you who you are, so to speak. These perks can vary from talking to plants and animals, body modifications, mental enhancements, &quot;TV in my head&quot;, enthralled spirits, empowered items and flat out new senses. <br /> So I see each unused spell control slot like wasted characterization space that could be used to tell something memorable about character in question [if npc], or a wasted opportunity to redefine your gameplay experience [if player]. It also helps with the whole Mage Monster thing, as the bigger your Gnosis, the more spell control you get to redefine yourself with, and the end result of your remodeling might be...thought provoking, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:42:29-07:00","id":1066330,"title":"","content":"How paranoid PCs are seems to follow a natural arc, from not paranoid at all (new to the game) to extreme panic paranoia (still learning the system) to the subtler and more insidious form of paranoia (familiarity).<br /> <br /> Remember, a Mage who walks around with active spells on them shines like a Christmas tree. Walking down a crowded street without them, another Mage won't likely notice you, but if you are wandering with active spells, it attracts notice. <br /> <br /> The truth is, there isn't much point keeping up spells like that constantly, especially given how much trouble it might attract and how unlikely the spells themselves are to actually protect you - not because the spells are likely to fail but because a given spell only protects against a narrow subset of issues. A Mind Shielding spell won't save you from Fate magic causing a car crash.<br /> <br /> Remember, the first lessons a Mage learns is that a shining beacon calls to people and that a Lie keeps things hidden and out of reach. Staying hidden and unnoticed is more important to staying safe than any wall or ward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T08:53:44-07:00","id":1066341,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but if you are like, really concerned about not glowing like a christmas tree, it's easy peasy to just veil them and be done with it. Between &quot;abandoning my cool toys that allow me to be super sexy, watch funny cat videos on the internet with my brain, thought drive my car and eat a perfect ramen soup at the same time&quot; and &quot;just casting a token effort veiling spell targeting all of my spells so people will fuck off&quot;, I rather see people choosing the second. I follow the idea that after you upgrade your living standards, you are going to be extremely unwilling to abandon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:00:39-07:00","id":1066346,"title":"","content":"&quot;Easy peasy&quot; if you have Prime 2+. Most Mages do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:05:34-07:00","id":1066350,"title":"","content":"I presume most PC Cabals will have Prime 2. If they do, chances are they will use Supernal Veil to cloak magic and Wards and Signs to improve their spell's withstand. Because dispel magic does suck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:08:58-07:00","id":1066352,"title":"","content":"Depends on the player and depends on the ST. If the player is used to dangerous STs who are actively trying to kill them at every turn, then obviously they are going to do everything in their power to make sure they are prepared for it. If you, as an ST, are constantly trying to kill your players at every turn, they <i>will </i>become paranoid - and justifiably so. If you gauge their opponents by their abilities and generally give them room to breathe, then they will probably ease up (or leave because they <i>like </i>being constantly in danger and feel like you're a bad ST who should feel bad.)<br /> <br /> That's been my experience anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:13:00-07:00","id":1066358,"title":"","content":"I think that &quot;spells created by my Arcanum&quot; fall under Arcanum's purview for purposes of what you can Veil? Like, Prime should allow you to veil &quot;any spell&quot;, while Spirit should be able to conceal effects of Spirit spells, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:29:21-07:00","id":1066368,"title":"","content":"I've got a PC cabal in my Ausgame that didn't have one character with it until recently. Even then, he couldn't really afford to cover all the spells everyone might have up all the time. Not without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd say hiding a Spirit spell from Mage Sight is way more the dominion of Prime, because the part you're hiding isn't any element of the Spirit arcanum. You're hiding that it's magic at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T09:35:54-07:00","id":1066382,"title":"","content":"My mage is hugely paranoid, it's something that comes up again and again in my game. The social constructs are mainly built to help alleviate fear of betrayal. Still, when you are good friends with someone who can change time, or re-design your memory, how can you not always feel a little suspicious towards them? What spell can you cast to alleviate that fear? If you're scared of your friends, my goodness, what about your enemies? My mage had a car fly out of nowhere, miles away from known danger, in an attempt to crush her like a bug. She had strange puppets spying on her sanctum in the woods. A slightly insane associate was murdered in a safehouse by a mage presumed dead. <br /> <br /> Paranoid yes, paralyzed no. Mages are bold and overconfident and quick to judge because they need to be to survive. And when they make horrifying mistakes they suck it up and carry on.. fun times.<br /> <br /> As a disclaimer, when I began playing WoD, many many moons ago, I swore I'd never play mage as I thought it was too complicated and boring. I no longer think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:04:09-07:00","id":1066412,"title":"","content":"A Cabal of 4 Gnosis 3 mages I see...<br /> <br /> Supernal Veil, Wards and Signs, Warding Gesture, Ward, Perfect Sympathy, Alter Mental Pattern and boosts to Resolve / Stamina / Composure are pretty common once a Cabal hits Gnosis 3+. Throw in a daily divination because why not?<br /> <br /> Before that... it *really* depens on the Mage or the Cabal. My players tend to be paranoid when shit hits the fan, but not so much before then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:15:15-07:00","id":1066424,"title":"","content":"To add: it's probably standard procedure (potentially even taught during initiation) to ward (and Ward) your Sanctum, because if there's one place you <i>need</i> to feel <i>absolutely secure and in control</i> in, it's your Sanctum. Casting a bunch of powerful protective spells (and relinquishing them to avoid having to Reach for every spell thereafter) wouldn't be out of the ordinary. It'd probably be <i>more</i> out of the ordinary to <i>not </i>do that \u2013 akin to not even having a handle on your front door, let alone a lock or peep-hole; just, like, a plank of wood.<br /> <br /> (by which I mean you don't need to be considered paranoid in order to protect your home)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:33:28-07:00","id":1066440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066382#post1066382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-words-</div> </div> </div> </div>My kind of jam.<br /> <br /> I've got stories of the other side of that, too; how a Mage being able to tell people what they are doesn't alleviate that deep, crushing sense of loneliness that comes from not being able to trust someone. <br /> <br /> Being a Mage is a delightful and special kind of hell; the kind you'd never give up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:40:03-07:00","id":1066445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1066305#post1066305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These people weren't any more or less &quot;stupid&quot; than any other human being. Brains are just garbage at predicting things they've never experienced.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GA7r0-zGfIw\" target=\"_blank\">It may me human nature to assume that the absence of anything bad happening means that what we do is safe. This is obviously wrong and a concerted effort is needed to root out those unnecessarily risky behaviors. This &quot;comfort zone&quot; mentality needs to be eliminated.</a><br /> <br /> That's a quote because the &quot;comfort zone&quot; mentality is part of human nature.<br /> <br /> Human beings are not optimized to be &quot;safe&quot; and thinking we are is silly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://quoteinvestigator.com/2013/04/06/fish-climb/\" target=\"_blank\">Everyone is a genius. But if you judge a fish by its ability to climb a tree, it will live its whole life believing that it is stupid.</a> -Albert Einstein<br /> <br /> <br /> And of Dark Archon is showing serious <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_swan_theory\" target=\"_blank\">black swan theory psychological bias</a> in saying:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065907#post1065907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't such people seen as careless and stupid? I certainly do see every person who do the things above as stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an unfair assessment and is wrong as a blanket statement, and has strong implications of condescension. Also I find the following assertion dubious because it seems to contradict <a href=\"https://www.quora.com/What-causes-human-carelessness\" target=\"_blank\">basic facts</a> <a href=\"https://authoritynutrition.com/12-graphs-that-show-why-people-get-fat/\" target=\"_blank\">found in</a> <a href=\"http://www.safetypartnersltd.com/7-most-common-causes-of-workplace-accidents/\" target=\"_blank\">human</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akrasia\" target=\"_blank\">nature</a>, and is likely either caused by inaccurately biased self-perception and the halo-effect on those associated with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063365-time-magic-ultimate-mystery-solver?p=1065907#post1065907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After probability of such event becomes too high in my opinion? Yes, I do. And all people I know do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also everyone on facebook is <i>stupid</i>? (<a href=\"https://www.techwalla.com/articles/the-purpose-of-facebook\" target=\"_blank\">the stated purpose of facebook is a place to share personal information, openly,</a> from pictures to what you are doing to what think about things, and how you feel at any moment) And *<u>all people</u> he knows thinks so too?? Unlikely.<br /> <br /> I can picture some mages putting on a shielding spell, maybe two, in the same way I picture some people grabbing an umbrella and spending 30 minutes listening to the traffic and weather reports before starting their commute.<br /> <br /> I can also picture some mages becoming doomsday prepper like, and I\u2019d expect that the percentage of those individuals to be similar to mundane population, and about as stigmatized, and that view is supported by canon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtA p. 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is that playing with people\u2019s sympathetic links has a real, tangible effect on their lives. The Wise look <a href=\"http://www.dictionary.com/browse/askance\" target=\"_blank\">askance</a> on those mages who endeavor to cull their own sympathetic \u201cvulnerabilities\u201d <u>with good reason</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Underlined for emphasis.<br /> <br /> That said, I also picture mages gearing up in a way analogous to fire fighters going into a burning building when they expect that level of trouble, or as a CSI team when a crime happens that needs investigation, complete with the magical equivalent of crime scene tap, collaboration in collecting samples, and over watch security of those investigating. If the mundanes have it figured out and you can find it in a simple google searchm it\u2019d be silly mages wouldn\u2019t have thought of it.<br /> <br /> Also warding your sanctum is the magical equivalent of checking all the locks are secure in your house, and making sure the alarm is armed.<br /> <br /> Magic is really just another level of what is mundane. It's like <a href=\"http://biblehub.com/luke/16-10.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Luke 16:10</a>, but with safety. The much being what you can do with magic, and the little being what you can mundanely accomplish.<br /> <br /> Posting here because this seems to better fit the topic the other thread has morphed into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 03-22-2017, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:48:31-07:00","id":1066452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066445#post1066445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GA7r0-zGfIw\" target=\"_blank\">It may me human nature to assume that the absence of anything bad happening means that what we do is safe. This is obviously wrong and a concerted effort is needed to root out those unnecessarily risky behaviors. This &quot;comfort zone&quot; mentality needs to be eliminated.</a><br /> <br /> That's a quote because the &quot;comfort zone&quot; mentality is part of human nature.<br /> <br /> Human beings are not optimized to be &quot;safe&quot; and thinking we are is silly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://quoteinvestigator.com/2013/04/06/fish-climb/\" target=\"_blank\">Everyone is a genius. But if you judge a fish by its ability to climb a tree, it will live its whole life believing that it is stupid.</a> -Albert Einstein</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear: I agree and was adding onto what you were saying, not arguing against it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:00:49-07:00","id":1066463,"title":"","content":"Less paranoid than a Hunter or Changeling, more paranoid than a Werewolf. WAY more paranoid than a Sin-Eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:01:02-07:00","id":1066464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066452#post1066452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be clear: I agree and was adding onto what you were saying, not arguing against it :P</div> </div> </div> </div>To also be clear, I should have added something that acknowledged that you agreed, because I knew. Sorry for the oversight. I included your quote not because I thought you disagreed but because you agreed and did so articulately.<br /> <br /> I meant your quote as a topic sentence but totally see why you thought I was responding to you. Again sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:07:28-07:00","id":1066472,"title":"","content":"Not very, especially once they realized that layering active magical effects was getting them noticed more than anything else. It isn't really very easy to just tell who is and isn't a mage out of dozens of people walking down the street assuming they aren't bringing attention (mundane or magical) to themselves. The only time they get paranoid is when they have a legitimate reason to be (i.e. they've pissed off someone/some group in particular, or they're diving into something that they know might be dangerous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-22-2017, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:09:02-07:00","id":1066473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066464#post1066464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant your quote as a topic sentence but totally see why you thought I was responding to you. Again sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool don't worry about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T11:55:37-07:00","id":1066500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066368#post1066368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a PC cabal in my Ausgame that didn't have one character with it until recently. Even then, he couldn't really afford to cover all the spells everyone might have up all the time. Not without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'd say hiding a Spirit spell from Mage Sight is way more the dominion of Prime, because the part you're hiding isn't any element of the Spirit arcanum. You're hiding that it's magic at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiding *from* Magic Sight is definitely Prime (and Death), which is why you can hide any spell no matter what Arcanum using Prime, but what I'm saying is not &quot;hiding from&quot;. It's using &quot;hiding a thing belonging to my Arcanum from everything else&quot;. You can Veil things so that they are hidden from things that fall under your Arcanum, *or* you can hide something that falls under your Arcanum from anything else. And I don't think there is anything more &quot;of your Arcanum&quot; than spells created by it, don't you think? I mean, you already can target spells with stuff like Hung Spell.<br /> <br /> As for not being able to hide all spells, I'm curious what stops your PC? If it's blank &quot;I can't afford potency to target that number of individual spells&quot;, use Area as a Scale instead of flat number of subjects, targeting every single spell in the room.<br /> Which brings me to another thing: if it's ok for Jake to layer himself with a Mind Shield, and it's ok for a Jane to layer herself with a Ghost Shield, and it's ok for Ruby to layer itself with Wards and Signs, what is so wrong about them saying &quot;Hey guys, I'm doing my yearly renewal of a Mind Shield, drop by our Sanctum and I will Reach so it covers all of us&quot;? Or even &quot;Hell, if I'm investing a Willpower Dot into a Mind Shield, then at least let's make it worth it, MIND SHIELD FOR EVERYONE&quot;?<br /> I see a lot of artificial barriers here that IMHO create a dissonance with the emergent gameplay coming from the spellcasting rules. Which I find funny, because I have a feeling that people would love Merits that mimick these spells, but would be in arms against functionally identical spells that were Safely Relinquished - which, in practice, turns them into Merits worth one XP that don't fall under protection of sanctity of merits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:04:10-07:00","id":1066505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066500#post1066500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiding *from* Magic Sight is definitely Prime (and Death), which is why you can hide any spell no matter what Arcanum using Prime, but what I'm saying is not &quot;hiding from&quot;. It's using &quot;hiding a thing belonging to my Arcanum from everything else&quot;. You can Veil things so that they are hidden from things that fall under your Arcanum, *or* you can hide something that falls under your Arcanum from anything else. And I don't think there is anything more &quot;of your Arcanum&quot; than spells created by it, don't you think? I mean, you already can target spells with stuff like Hung Spell.<br /> <br /> As for not being able to hide all spells, I'm curious what stops your PC? If it's blank &quot;I can't afford potency to target that number of individual spells&quot;, use Area as a Scale instead of flat number of subjects, targeting every single spell in the room.<br /> Which brings me to another thing: if it's ok for Jake to layer himself with a Mind Shield, and it's ok for a Jane to layer herself with a Ghost Shield, and it's ok for Ruby to layer itself with Wards and Signs, what is so wrong about them saying &quot;Hey guys, I'm doing my yearly renewal of a Mind Shield, drop by our Sanctum and I will Reach so it covers all of us&quot;? Or even &quot;Hell, if I'm investing a Willpower Dot into a Mind Shield, then at least let's make it worth it, MIND SHIELD FOR EVERYONE&quot;?<br /> I see a lot of artificial barriers here that IMHO create a dissonance with the emergent gameplay coming from the spellcasting rules. Which I find funny, because I have a feeling that people would love Merits that mimick these spells, but would be in arms against functionally identical spells that were Safely Relinquished - which, in practice, turns them into Merits worth one XP that don't fall under protection of sanctity of merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. A Death spell for example might be able to target things related to death, but the spell in and of itself falls under the purview of Prime, not Death. You could probably use Death to veil Death spells (or any other spell really) from dead things, but the spell, the actual mystical components that change reality, that's Prime. To veil <i>that</i> from everything you'd need Prime.<br /> <br /> Also, that isn't how area Scale works. Area targets the literal area (and everything in it) and doesn't move unless the targeted area does, which would take some pretty crazy magic to do. If you cast an area spell to veil all spells within an area, all spells within the area would be veiled, but once they left that area they'd no longer be hidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-22-2017, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:06:19-07:00","id":1066509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066500#post1066500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip*<br /> As for not being able to hide all spells, I'm curious what stops your PC? If it's blank &quot;I can't afford potency to target that number of individual spells&quot;, use Area as a Scale instead of flat number of subjects, targeting every single spell in the room.<br /> *snip*</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Dave somewhere (sorry, not sure where) state that using Area as Scale will make the spell work for *that* Area? So that'd work so long as you remained in the covered area, but once you step out, the Veiling effect would drop. And if somebody not in the initial area walked into it, their spells would be veiled. Which actually solves the problem of being constantly dinged when in Mage-heavy areas like Consilium; one of the higher ups just throws up a large Area Veiling spell over the room.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops, got ninja-ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1897,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","user":"ffanxii4ever","date":". 03-22-2017, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:10:53-07:00","id":1066515,"title":"","content":"Aren't you the person who said that it's ok to make Shield Spells that protect you from &quot;spells of a given Arcanum&quot;? Because for me, it's logical that if you can Shield from it [because it's a part of your Arcanum], then it follows that you can Veil it, because it's a part of your Arcanum.<br /> Then you also get a Suppress Aura spell...which makes spells on the subject appear as, well, dead, making you look like a Sleeper with not a tingle of magic around you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:19:13-07:00","id":1066519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066515#post1066515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't you the person who said that it's ok to make Shield Spells that protect you from &quot;spells of a given Arcanum&quot;? Because for me, it's logical that if you can Shield from it [because it's a part of your Arcanum], then it follows that you can Veil it, because it's a part of your Arcanum.<br /> Then you also get a Suppress Aura spell...which makes spells on the subject appear as, well, dead, making you look like a Sleeper with not a tingle of magic around you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said <i>kinda,</i> giving the example that Mental Shield can let you Clash against all mind affecting abilities. It just so happens that that is literally all Mind has, even if it technically takes different forms (mind control, illusions, emotions, etc.). I then went to say that even for the things where you couldn't, you could prep shields for an arcanas most commonly used effects (i.e. shields against lightning or fire for Forces). That is not the same as creating a shield against or veiling raw magic, which is what you're suggesting.<br /> <br /> The other arcana can veil even spells (probably?) from things in their purview, but not magic itself as that is the purview of Prime. You could probably use Incognito Presence on spells, shrouding them from mental detection that way, you could use Life to hide them from living things, or Death to hide them from the undead, but you can't really completely hide magic from everything with one spell without Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-22-2017, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:26:53-07:00","id":1066523,"title":"","content":"Ghost Shield also flat out blocks &quot;Death Spells&quot;. Mind Shield also literally states &quot;Mind Spells&quot;. Ephemeral Shield also goes out of it's way to mention &quot;Spirit Spells&quot;.<br /> Death also has Suppress Aura, which literally dampens subject's aura and that of all spells that affect it, making them register as a nonmagical Sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-22-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:31:43-07:00","id":1066524,"title":"","content":"I think the discussion about whether you need Prime 2 to avoid your protective spells setting off other mages Peripheral Mage Sight is probably interesting enough to justify its own thread? One thing I have been curious about is the extent to which Mages peddle spells as services for sale to each other. Not so much for cash of course, but favours, mana, knowledge or other spells. <br /> <br /> For example, If your Cabal lacks someone with the capability to cast Anti-Spirit wards on their sanctum, how likely or practical is it that they could get a friendly mage to provide some? I am envisioning a small number of mages who regularly provide such services around the community for a fee?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:32:48-07:00","id":1066525,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say that Death could Veil a Death spell, and same for the rest of the arcana. Prime can just do it without having to worry about which arcana it's Veiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:34:05-07:00","id":1066526,"title":"","content":"Give them something worth at least 1XP for their trouble (to compensate for their Willpower loss), and if they aren't doing community service, you probably would need to give them something based on rarity of the spell in question to make it worth their time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:34:05-07:00","id":1066527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066523#post1066523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Shield also flat out blocks &quot;Death Spells&quot;. Mind Shield also literally states &quot;Mind Spells&quot;. Ephemeral Shield also goes out of it's way to mention &quot;Spirit Spells&quot;.<br /> Death also has Suppress Aura, which literally dampens subject's aura and that of all spells that affect it, making them register as a nonmagical Sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those arcana <i>effect</i> things falling within the same purview you are shielding, but they are not, in and of themselves that purview. A Death spell is a <i>spell</i> (which falls under Primes purview) that causes an <i>effect</i> that relates to Death. Using Death you can shield yourself against all effects relating to Death, even those caused by Death spells, but the spell itself is just that, a spell (belonging to Prime).<br /> <br /> That said, as has been pointed out elsewhere, Death is apparently a bit of a special case (see Shadow Flesh). It does shit that straight up goes against the stated workings of the arcana under some justification that it's inherently apart of shit or some junk. Honestly, I'd just say screw it and make everything work the way it seems like it's supposed to but I think we're discussing rules as written so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-22-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T12:34:09-07:00","id":1066528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066524#post1066524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, If your Cabal lacks someone with the capability to cast Anti-Spirit wards on their sanctum, how likely or practical is it that they could get a friendly mage to provide some? I am envisioning a small number of mages who regularly provide such services around the community for a fee?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty likely. Heck, with Status you don't even have to pay, you just requisition it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T14:07:57-07:00","id":1066570,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly non-paranoid for Gnosis 5 first Degree Masters/third degree Adepts, but we are hubristic as shit and as we spend so much of our time in either alternate dimensions, alternate timelines, or on other planets, we aren't really anywhere long enough to make enemies that actively hunt us. We also always try to honor our cabal's name &quot;Ex Tenebris&quot;, i.e. never let anyone notice you are involved to begin with. Still, our carelessness has made us walk into a trap by some Sleeper Hunters once already.<br /> <br /> ... though looking at our active spells right now we have used our new Sleepwalker Retainer to park some defensive spells like Wards &amp; Signs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T21:09:09-07:00","id":1066694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066570#post1066570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surprisingly non-paranoid for Gnosis 5 first Degree Masters/third degree Adepts, but we are hubristic as shit and as we spend so much of our time in either alternate dimensions, alternate timelines, or on other planets, we aren't really anywhere long enough to make enemies that actively hunt us. We also always try to honor our cabal's name &quot;Ex Tenebris&quot;, i.e. never let anyone notice you are involved to begin with. Still, our carelessness has made us walk into a trap by some Sleeper Hunters once already.<br /> <br /> ... though looking at our active spells right now we have used our new Sleepwalker Retainer to park some defensive spells like Wards &amp; Signs.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, you play mages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I have an analogy to demonstrate where I would put mages. I live in a place where ants are common. I could spread ant killer around the yard regularly but I don't. I use ant killer when I see large mounds that appear to be spreading. I spray around the openings that lead into my house regularly. My home is free of ants which is what I want and I don't waste time or resources on pests that aren't bothering me.<br /> <br /> Mages seek out danger or else they would be sleepwalkers instead. I suspect a given mage has one method to provide general protection, which may not be a spell, and adds spells when expecting trouble. I find it hard to believe it would be common for a mage to throw up a bunch of shields to go buy a gallon of milk under normal circumstances. Players in stories are more likely to be in situations where trouble is to be expected than grocery shopping. Safe places are probably tin foil hat paranoid though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T01:58:28-07:00","id":1066740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066445#post1066445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of Dark Archon is showing serious...</div> </div> </div> </div>You are saying many smart words, which don't cover up the simple fact: forgetting to fasten your seat belt or ignoring it is dangerously stupid. If I forget to do it, I am just as stupid. But most of the time, I fasten my seat belt, don't run across the roads, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066445#post1066445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also everyone on facebook is <i>stupid</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>That really depends on that they are storing at Facebook. If they store important or dangerous or private information? Yes, they are. <br /> <br /> You are seem to misunderstand a thing: if all people have cognitive biases, that just make us all stupid on some level. And we all are. Not being able to care for the future, to predict it and act with it in mind is very <b>definition </b>of stupid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066445#post1066445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic is really just another level of what is mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. Mages aren't living mundane lives. They may try to, but that's not going to stick, because they have Obsessions, and those Obsessions will lead them into the dangerous places. They will create enemies for them. And even if they tried to just live their lifes, there is a whole world out here which is <i>dangerous</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T02:04:32-07:00","id":1066742,"title":"","content":"My Mage is so paranoid he just changed his Shadow Name, because it was getting too commonly know, is going to avoid saying his new one as much as possible, and is desperately studying Prime as fast as he can so that in addition to being able to teleport, establish SEP fields, and mind-fuck people, we can also hide all of his Magic from detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:49:47-07:00","id":1066764,"title":"","content":"My understanding of the veiling practice is that you can veil the effects of your spells under the same arcanum such that they won't trigger peripheral mage sight. However, active mage sight will still detect them if the Prime version isn't used. Or, in other words, the normal veiling is sufficient for most mages since it's pms that you're going to be worried about and not ams. If a mage is using ams then you're going to know already that someone is potentially looking for you since his ams will trigger YOUR pms.<br /> <br /> As to paranoia, my group usually doesn't go around with defensive spells in place unless we are out and about. Then we might have one up each. If we know we are going into battle, then we add more. As to our sanctum, it has its guards and wards. This is mostly coming from the fact that we have low gnosis (2 for most of the gameplay so far, the others only just recently got 3), so spell control is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:21:08-07:00","id":1066791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066764#post1066764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If a mage is using ams then you're going to know already that someone is potentially looking for you since his ams will trigger YOUR pms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it correct?<br /> Edit: I think it is. But it might be dependent of the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-23-2017, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:54:40-07:00","id":1066911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066740#post1066740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are saying many smart words, which don't cover up the simple fact: forgetting to fasten your seat belt or ignoring it is dangerously stupid. If I forget to do it, I am just as stupid. But most of the time, I fasten my seat belt, don't run across the roads, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of missing the point.<br /> <br /> Sure, forgetting to fasten your seat-belt or ignoring it is stupid.<br /> <br /> This doesn't change the fact that lots of people don't do it, anyway, DESPITE it being stupid.<br /> <br /> Lots of people use the same password for every online service they're a member of, or use &quot;PASSWORD&quot; as their password, too. More or less <i>everyone</i> drives faster than the speed limit, habitually ignores traffic laws, and otherwise engages in risky driving behavior. The OVERWHELMING MAJORITY of people just randomly tune in to whatever news broadcast informs their own political position rather than actually becoming informed on the issues that affect them.<br /> <br /> People do stupid things, every single day, and this will never ever stop.<br /> <br /> Police Officers get caught flat-footed when involving themselves in a situation that they don't <i>think</i> will be violent. Soldiers in a war zone yell &quot;SNIPER!&quot; and take cover, rather than living every single second of the their day as if they could get arbitrarily killed by someone half a mile away. People give out their banking account information to people they shouldn't, give out their social security numbers to some scammer on the phone, and do a thousand other things that they <i>know</i> they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Those are things that people do.<br /> <br /> Mages are people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:59:40-07:00","id":1066919,"title":"","content":"Dark Archon has made a habit of missing the forest for the trees if it can prolong the argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:38:38-07:00","id":1066949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066505#post1066505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, that isn't how area Scale works. Area targets the literal area (and everything in it) and doesn't move unless the targeted area does, which would take some pretty crazy magic to do. If you cast an area spell to veil all spells within an area, all spells within the area would be veiled, but once they left that area they'd no longer be hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066509#post1066509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't Dave somewhere (sorry, not sure where) state that using Area as Scale will make the spell work for *that* Area? So that'd work so long as you remained in the covered area, but once you step out, the Veiling effect would drop. And if somebody not in the initial area walked into it, their spells would be veiled. Which actually solves the problem of being constantly dinged when in Mage-heavy areas like Consilium; one of the higher ups just throws up a large Area Veiling spell over the room.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whoops, got ninja-ed</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Area Factor works. You aren't targeting the Area, you are targeting everything inside target area:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core Rulebook, page 113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines <br /> how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell <br /> effect to anyone or anything within. A mage cannot single out <br /> specific subjects in the declared space unless she uses the spell <br /> Warding Gesture</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave also explained how Area Factor works multiple times:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page65\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page65\"> Ask a simple question, Awakened edition - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page65\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page65 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I reopen the thread : (Original author : Archmage Joda) To restart : Q1 : Camelot was created by Imperium Rite or Practice ? </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912686-scale-and-range\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912686-scale-and-range\"> Scale and Range - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912686-scale-and-range\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912686-scale-and-range </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> If you cast a spell using advanced scale (to affect everyone in a house, for example), do you still need to meet range requirements (IE, touch, sensory) for all individual subjects affected? </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page76\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page76\"> Ask a simple question, Awakened edition - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page76\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page76 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I reopen the thread : (Original author : Archmage Joda) To restart : Q1 : Camelot was created by Imperium Rite or Practice ? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Only thing about spells leaving area that I remember was the thing about stuff in Verges/Demesnes not provoking Paradox, which was specified that spells aimed outside the Paradox free zone aren't paradox free anymore: <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges\"> Exarchate Verges - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> [B] Isn't the Reach a meaningless benefit? If your spells are immune to paradox you essentially have infinite reach. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:44:19-07:00","id":1067005,"title":"","content":"Actually both ways are valid interpretations, depending on exactly what you want your spell to do &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:16:21-07:00","id":1067026,"title":"","content":"They aren't different &quot;interpretations&quot;, they are using different set of factors. One thing is setting a specific &quot;space&quot; as a Subject, and another is using Area Scale Factor to target all subjects that can be affected by the spell. Two distinct and different spells, using different levers and spellcasting factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:16:27-07:00","id":1067027,"title":"","content":"Ah, that would explain why I was thinking that; anywho, enough of the tangent, my bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:24:21-07:00","id":1067031,"title":"","content":"Like, imagine that you are a Space Mage who want, for whatever reason, target a &quot;Church&quot; location. You set your Subject to &quot;Church&quot;, and then make sure your Scale is enough to encompass the whole Church [size of the biggest Subject]. Then you make sure that you can touch (touch range) or perceive (Sensory Range) at least one part of the Church (if, say, the Church is sunk into a desert and only a small part of it is visible, it's enough). <br /> <br /> However, you could also make a spell where &quot;Church&quot; is only viable target, and then cast a large Area spell that will affect every single compatible &quot;Church&quot; space location inside the area. <br /> I assume that doing either (targeting a single Church Location, and All Churches Inside Spell Radius) would demand you to understand Space, in order to figure out what exactly a &quot;Church location&quot; *is*. <br /> Which still won't stop your Mastigos from casually looking at a church (as in, a building), tapping it with their hand and making everyone inside insane with a large Area Spell that makes people go Insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:24:59-07:00","id":1067032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067026#post1067026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't different &quot;interpretations&quot;, they are using different set of factors. One thing is setting a specific &quot;space&quot; as a Subject, and another is using Area Scale Factor to target all subjects that can be affected by the spell. Two distinct and different spells, using different levers and spellcasting factors.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe he refers to possible applications of area casting<br /> 1. Cast on everything that is inside. Afterward everything that was present at site will be affected no matter where it goes.<br /> 2. Cast on area to change it properties in such a way that affect everything that is inside. When you leave you are not affected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:27:49-07:00","id":1067035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067031#post1067031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, imagine that you are a Space Mage who want, for whatever reason, target a &quot;Church&quot; location. You set your Subject to &quot;Church&quot;, and then make sure your Scale is enough to encompass the whole Church [size of the biggest Subject]. Then you make sure that you can touch (touch range) or perceive (Sensory Range) at least one part of the Church (if, say, the Church is sunk into a desert and only a small part of it is visible, it's enough).<br /> <br /> However, you could also make a spell where &quot;Church&quot; is only viable target, and then cast a large Area spell that will affect every single compatible &quot;Church&quot; space location inside the area.<br /> I assume that doing either (targeting a single Church Location, and All Churches Inside Spell Radius) would demand you to understand Space, in order to figure out what exactly a &quot;Church location&quot; *is*.<br /> Which still won't stop your Mastigos from casually looking at a church (as in, a building), tapping it with their hand and making everyone inside insane with a large Area Spell that makes people go Insane.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, now I see it. It was also my gut feeling about needing a space arcanum for my second option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:34:09-07:00","id":1067039,"title":"","content":"I think that the 2nd one would target a Subject of &quot;Space&quot;, with size determined by Scale, which is different configuration of spell factors than using Area to determine how many Subjects got affected. <br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Subject: This Room&quot; creates a &quot;zone&quot; or a &quot;cloud&quot; to use visual representation that affects the room itself, while &quot;Subjects: Everyone inside this Room&quot; creates a &quot;pulse&quot; that checks once for everyone inside the area and then doesn't bother with their location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:38:30-07:00","id":1067043,"title":"","content":"You would need cast a conjunctional for that. Forces 5, Life 1 - burn all humans inside the church and nothing else.<br /> Edit: Space or Fate could help too with their Keys","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:52:14-07:00","id":1067050,"title":"","content":"I think that without fate you can't specify who gets hit with an area spell, that's what the targets option is for. Space can restrict who can use it's portals and the like by keys, but that is for who can use, not targeted by it.<br /> I don't think life is needed either way. You don't need life to hurt a living thing, and you don't need life to use fate to only target living things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:59:11-07:00","id":1067060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067026#post1067026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't different &quot;interpretations&quot;, they are using different set of factors. One thing is setting a specific &quot;space&quot; as a Subject, and another is using Area Scale Factor to target all subjects that can be affected by the spell. Two distinct and different spells, using different levers and spellcasting factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good, so you agree with me and just wanted to be overly pedantic about it. Hazza.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i612.photobucket.com/albums/tt206/cheryl_martin1/RollingEyesSmiley5.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:01:02-07:00","id":1067062,"title":"","content":"Fate is extremely broad and thus reaally good at specifying targets. <br /> Lets say you stand in front of a building and can't see whats inside but want to burn all humans and only them. You can use fate component and say &quot;only humans&quot; or life &quot;only humans&quot; since they fall under its purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:07:41-07:00","id":1067068,"title":"","content":"Page 113 says the only way to specify who you target in an area spell is via fate magic warding gesture.<br /> Since it uses the term only I think that life wouldnt help.<br /> Ninja: Meant to edit in previous post as a reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:26:54-07:00","id":1067093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066949#post1066949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's not how Area Factor works. You aren't targeting the Area, you are targeting everything inside target area:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dave also explained how Area Factor works multiple times:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page65\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page65</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912686-scale-and-range\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...cale-and-range</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition/page76\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...edition/page76</a><br /> <br /> Only thing about spells leaving area that I remember was the thing about stuff in Verges/Demesnes not provoking Paradox, which was specified that spells aimed outside the Paradox free zone aren't paradox free anymore:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/919627-exarchate-verges\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...archate-verges</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, none of what you linked contradicts what I've said. I said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1066505#post1066505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Area targets the literal area (<b>and everything in it</b>) and doesn't move unless the targeted area does, which would take some pretty crazy magic to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It targets the area and every valid target in it, <i>but</i> the book also goes on to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw pg. 113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines<br /> how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell<br /> effect to anyone or anything within.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we know that it applies spell effects to those <i>within</i> the boundaries of the spell. We also know that know spells constantly check to see if all parameters have still remained the same, and if the parameters change, it potentially changes if the spell still affects them or not. This was confirmed by Dave when talking about Potency and whether raising or lowering of Withstand ratings alter whether a target is or isn't affected by a spell.<br /> <br /> So if the spell effect of an area spell only applies to those within it, and that spell constantly checks to see if all requirements have been met, <i>and</i> someone under the affect of such a spell leaves the range of its stated boundaries then the spell should update itself and apply to them as if they were outside of the spells area of effect (which they are) and cease to affect them at all.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, I can see where your argument is coming from and I don't discount it. I believe it's possible you might be right but under a strict interpretation of how we know spells work I'm fairly sure that I'm right on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-23-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:32:29-07:00","id":1067096,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an effect of Space Magic, not Area Factor. It also sounds like Dynamic Magic, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:41:32-07:00","id":1067100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067096#post1067096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an effect of Space Magic, not Area Factor. It also sounds like Dynamic Magic, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> Lets take turning people into frogs for example. You cast a spell on a room turning everyone in it into frogs with a duration of a day. The people inside are immediately turned into frogs. What happens when others walk in? Is the effect constant or does it function like damaging/healing spells over time and recast every ritual casting interval? If it had been targeted to the people in the room the spell would be <i>on</i> them. It would follow them around regardless of where they go and constantly apply its effect. Instead you cast on the area, that room, so instead of the effect following the people turned into frogs it effects the area (and all valid targets within it). But since you didn't target the people specifically, the effect doesn't follow them, since it sticks with the original target, the area (and those within it). If the people turned frogs leave then they are no longer within the area, and since the magic only turns (and keeps) people within the area frogs, leaving it would remove you from the spell effect.<br /> <br /> Now if they went back into that room they, and anyone else who went in would again be turned into frogs while in there until that day is up and the spell effect ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:41:48-07:00","id":1067101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067096#post1067096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an effect of Space Magic, not Area Factor. It also sounds like Dynamic Magic, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has worked like this since 1e. You could, for example, cast Supernal Veil on your Sanctum such that all magic within is veiled. Likewise for the area inside your car, and it would move with the car without Dynamics or Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:49:15-07:00","id":1067111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067101#post1067101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has worked like this since 1e. You could, for example, cast Supernal Veil on your Sanctum such that all magic within is veiled. Likewise for the area inside your car, and it would move with the car without Dynamics or Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Just like when you're casting protective spells over your Sanctum to fuck over intruders. It only applies while inside the Sanctum, if they run away the affects don't follow them out the door and remain on them indefinitely (assuming your Sanctum guarding spell had an indefinite Duration) until they get them dispelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-23-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:50:02-07:00","id":1067187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067100#post1067100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really.<br /> <br /> Lets take turning people into frogs for example. You cast a spell on a room turning everyone in it into frogs with a duration of a day. The people inside are immediately turned into frogs. What happens when others walk in? Is the effect constant or does it function like damaging/healing spells over time and recast every ritual casting interval? If it had been targeted to the people in the room the spell would be <i>on</i> them. It would follow them around regardless of where they go and constantly apply its effect. Instead you cast on the area, that room, so instead of the effect following the people turned into frogs it effects the area (and all valid targets within it). But since you didn't target the people specifically, the effect doesn't follow them, since it sticks with the original target, the area (and those within it). If the people turned frogs leave then they are no longer within the area, and since the magic only turns (and keeps) people within the area frogs, leaving it would remove you from the spell effect.<br /> <br /> Now if they went back into that room they, and anyone else who went in would again be turned into frogs while in there until that day is up and the spell effect ends.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So ritual interval would be restricted to healing and damaging? Weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:08:49-07:00","id":1067225,"title":"","content":"No clue what this has to do with paranoia, but it isn't complicated. Scale has a few different options. Targeting people or chairs, or whatever, in a room uses number of subjects. Targeting the space the room occupies uses area of effect. Targeting the actual room uses size of subject which is more relevant for something that moves like a car.<br /> <br /> A pedagogic example is if you make a house invisible using area instead of subject and blow up the house the debris outside of the area the house used to occupy is visible. Using subject means all the debris remains invisible.<br /> <br /> Ritual interval is not restricted to healing or damage. A spell that switches a person's sex while in a room has an interval and sex is switched back and forth if a person remains in the room for a long duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T16:23:56-07:00","id":1067229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067225#post1067225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ritual interval is not restricted to healing or damage. A spell that switches a person's sex while in a room has an interval and sex is switched back and forth if a person remains in the room for a long duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends.<br /> First off, such an effect is most likely not Lasting. That means it won't repeat at the ritual interval because it already takes effect during the ritual interval.<br /> Secondly, if the change is Lasting the spell would most likely be designed to change the sex of the subject to a specific sex. That means the subject's sex would practically be unchanged after the initial effect since the spell would &quot;change&quot; the sex into the same sex every ritual interval. Only if the spell is deliberately designed to change male to female <i>and</i> female to male would it be able to change back and forth.<br /> <br /> Only spells with an instantaneous effect will trigger every ritual interval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:02:16-07:00","id":1067244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067187#post1067187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So ritual interval would be restricted to healing and damaging? Weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends. To be fair, damage and healing are the odd men out here. They're the exceptions to the normal rules, probably because damage over time, assuming it was a constant effect, would be pretty busted. Even a 1 bashing tick over a scene would be a death sentence for everything that can't regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:35:40-07:00","id":1067258,"title":"","content":"I'm going to bow out of the conversation, mostly because I feel that we have presented our perspectives on it and only thing left is to agree or disagree. Thanks for a civil discussion, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:15:51-07:00","id":1067309,"title":"","content":"You wake up in the morning, you get dressed, brush your teeth, maybe you eat breakfast, shower, check the weather, check your messages (e-mail, text, voice mail), maybe you feed your pets, maybe you say prayers or strap on a bullet proof vest and gun, whatever you do as part of your morning routine as long as the spell falls under your ruling Arcana or is a rote and doesn't require ritual casting it is no different than doing any of the real world things you as a person do in the morning.<br /> \u200bFor paranoia all that matters is will you set of the pms of any unknown, potentially hostile Mages you pass. If the answer is no then we are quibbling over approximately fifteen minutes of time.<br /> \u200bI would also point out that you are more likely to die in an auto accident than at the hands of a Banisher, Mad or Seer, so if in the same time it takes to buckle up and check your mirrors you can cast a spell that ensures you won't be killed when someone else runs a stop sign, wouldn't you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:06:37-07:00","id":1067405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067229#post1067229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends.<br /> First off, such an effect is most likely not Lasting. That means it won't repeat at the ritual interval because it already takes effect during the ritual interval.<br /> Secondly, if the change is Lasting the spell would most likely be designed to change the sex of the subject to a specific sex. That means the subject's sex would practically be unchanged after the initial effect since the spell would &quot;change&quot; the sex into the same sex every ritual interval. Only if the spell is deliberately designed to change male to female <i>and</i> female to male would it be able to change back and forth.<br /> <br /> Only spells with an instantaneous effect will trigger every ritual interval.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not create a spell to do anything like that so I'm not familiar with the particulars, but for pedagogy I was thinking of an instantaneous effect that turns male to female and female to male although I have to admit that it probably wouldn't be Lasting, therefore not instantaneous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:37:28-07:00","id":1067611,"title":"","content":"So DaveB posted this on rpgnet mage 2nd ed question thread in Jan <i>&quot;If your spell cloaks everyone in an area, it drops off them whenever they leave it (but also starts on anyone who enters it). If you cast it using number of subjects, it sticks to them after they split up.<br /> <br /> It's one of the main tactical choices you face in advanced play. There's times you'll want to go for one or the other. &quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:09:06-07:00","id":1067700,"title":"","content":"That's made pretty clear on the book, from when you choose Area of Effect to cast on a number of people or just the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T00:38:06-07:00","id":1068210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1067700#post1067700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's made pretty clear on the book, from when you choose Area of Effect to cast on a number of people or just the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not that clear if numerous people have different ideas about it. Having a aoe spell drop of people who leave the area isn't spelled out, hence why the confusion earlier. It seems to happen a lot in mage (i still dont understand combined spells 100% yet) that the wording is rather confusing and its not the first time there has been a reply of &quot;Its very clear blah blah&quot; when its not been that clear at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-26-2017, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T01:21:25-07:00","id":1068216,"title":"","content":"What do you think about universal '+1 Reach: Change relative anchor point of Area of Effect.'? You could make it around a traveling mage, an item or vehicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T22:11:41-07:00","id":1069091,"title":"","content":"My Dreamspeaker uses mage armor (Life) and a Mind Shield daily. Everything else is &quot;as needed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:34:10-07:00","id":1072808,"title":"","content":"In 1st edition, my Mage generally keeps up Mage Armor all day. Never know when you could be in a car accident, or attacked by a mugger, or blasted by lightning.... 2nd ed makes that impossible, but that's OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11852-arcane_pozhar","name":"Arcane_Pozhar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T23:26:46-07:00","id":1072964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane_Pozhar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066206-how-paranoid-are-your-mages?p=1072808#post1072808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1st edition, my Mage generally keeps up Mage Armor all day. Never know when you could be in a car accident, or attacked by a mugger, or blasted by lightning.... 2nd ed makes that impossible, but that's OK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to the ritual casting mechanics in 1e one of my players had a potency 50+ ward on him at all times. (magically inscreased skills/stats and rotes equals alot of dice esp with fate too). After reading various npc cabal info that said the have potency 5-6 wards/bans around sanctums it seemed really stupid. Hence all my npc's had to have similarly high potency defences as why wouldnt you if you could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T01:57:54-07:00","id":1073001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane_Pozhar</strong> <a href=\"